  "interfaces": {
    "finite_scope": "All C-markings generating An, without an omission-transitivity or connected-prefix restriction except the justified A6 rank4 census.",
    "new_complete_runs": "A7, A8, A10 through subgroup-order cutoffs11,14,20. Every transitive proper prefix is retained and extended; actual ambient group equality selects An.",
    "A6": "Accepted Topic D excludes all rank3; accepted L047 excludes connected rank4; simplicity and IP give connectedness; retained Whiston bound gives rank<=4.",
    "A5_A9": "Complete accepted L071 remaining censuses give the precise rank rows, including all higher zero rows.",
    "A11_A14": "Complete accepted L071 alternating census. In particular every rank6/7 marking of A12 is excluded, not merely selected types.",
    "existence": "Accepted whole L038 supplies every rank3..floor((n-1)/2) for all n>=12, with its exact actual construction and contraction closure. Its three earlier seeds are retained existence+IP inputs, not the upper theorem being recovered.",
    "end_criterion": "McMullen-Schulte Proposition2E16 remains an explicit retained theorem input; this packet does not claim a new proof of that external criterion.",
    "code": "enumerate_even.g and checks.g are unchanged accepted L071 bytes; check.py is new. GAP exact operations remain software premises.",
    "first_run_encoding": "The first-run stdout bytes are preserved under author_first_runs. Acquiring them into author_validation normalizes text newlines; report.json explicitly distinguishes original input hashes and normalized source hashes.",
    "closure": "Complete mathematical proofs and required finite executions of acquired inputs remain dependencies; no prior complete enumeration was restarted."
  },
  "contributions": "Known small rank values retain source attribution. The new work consists of missing complete degree7/8/10 executions, guarded full-IP checking, and exact noncircular principal interfaces. Root requested the A12 all-marking clarification and assigned the scope; no new mathematical idea or code for these executions was supplied by the distinct reviewer."
